  "design": {
    "entrance": "Guide rails draw on, then six horizontal slats of the extruded titanium title slide in from alternating sides, out of depth, locking into alignment one by one with a crisp mechanical snap.",
    "reveal": "The final slat locks on the impact frame: a cold seam flash runs along each joint and a narrow silver-blue highlight cuts across the chamfered edges.",
    "camera": "Slight three-quarter angle that squares up with a measured dolly; micro-jolt on each lock.",
    "material": "Cold brushed titanium: anisotropic brushed texture, flat chamfer bevel, narrow high-exponent silver-blue specular, cool environment reflection, dark gunmetal sides.",
    "exit": "The slats close like blinds - each band collapses to a thin line in sequence - and the rails retract."
  },
  "fusion_notes": [
    "Slats are rectangle-masked copies of the single Renderer3D output, each moved by its own Transform. If you change the title size or line count, adjust the slat masks' Center/Height (SlatNShape) so the bands still cover the letters."
  ],
